**PR description:**

> **Finance: only keep https issuer URLs as catalog sources** (audit finding L1, Low)
>
> **Problem.** The card catalog refresh stores source URLs written by the AI model and renders them as links (`catalog/page.tsx:161`).
> - `issuerSources()` (`refresh.ts:60-75`) checked only the hostname, so `javascript://chase.com/%0Aalert(1)` was accepted.
> - When a product had no `sourceDomains`, the model's URLs were stored with no check at all (`refresh.ts:143`).
> - React 19.3 rewrites `javascript:` hrefs, so this is hardening against prompt injection, not a live XSS.
>
> **Change.**
> - `issuerSources()` now requires `https:` as well as the issuer domain.
> - With no `sourceDomains`, only https URLs from the search provider's own sources count. URLs written by the model are ignored.
> - The catalog page filters out non-https links again at render time.
>
> **Behaviour note.** A user-added product with no domains and no provider sources now fails with "No source … was found". Seed entries and the add form both require at least one domain, so this shouldn't happen in practice.
>
> **Tests.** `tests/card-catalog.test.ts` checks that `javascript:`, `data:`, `http:` and `https://evil.com` URLs are rejected, `https://www.chase.com` is kept, and the no-domains path keeps only https.
>
> Reviewed by household-reviewer (approve) and challenger (ship). The challenger also confirmed Vertex grounding redirect URLs are still accepted.
