**PR description:**

> **Crypto: pin the AES-GCM auth tag to 16 bytes on decrypt** (audit finding L2, Low)
>
> **Problem.** `vault.ts` (document vault) and `secret-box.ts` (stored SimpleFIN access URL) called `setAuthTag()` without pinning the tag length. On Node 22, a 4-byte prefix of a valid tag still decrypts. That makes forgery much easier for anyone who can write ciphertext rows. Exploiting it needs write access to the database, hence Low.
>
> **Change.** Both decrypt paths pass `{ authTagLength: 16 }` to `createDecipheriv` and reject any tag that isn't 16 bytes before `setAuthTag`. Existing rows still decrypt, because `createCipheriv` always wrote 16-byte tags.
>
> **Tests.** New `tests/crypto-tag.test.ts`:
> - round trips for both;
> - a fresh nonce on every seal;
> - truncated tags and a flipped tag bit are rejected.
>
> The truncation cases fail on the old code.
>
> Reviewed by household-reviewer (approve) and challenger (ship). These are the only two `createDecipheriv` call sites.
>
